
This directory contains test bundles for randomized testing.
Each file contains a number of related ASN.1 types with variations in
contstraints that are intended to affect encoding and parsing.

 * Lines consisting of comments only are ignored.

 * The ASN.1 type can be written with "T ::=" prefix or without it, in which
   case it will be added automatically. It is done to simplify manual
   testing with ./check-bundles.sh -t <type>. For example,
        ./check-bundles.sh -t INTEGER
   is equivalent to
        ./check-bundles.sh -t "T ::= INTEGER"

 * By default, the random value generator attempts to generate values
   limited to very roughly to around 128 bytes. If huge values are desired
   (perhaps due to large constraints), the RMAX=<size> setting can be specified
   in the ASN.1 comments:

        T ::= VisibleString (SIZE(64000))    -- RMAX=64000
   
Large random values (RMAX >= 16384) use eight iterations per encoding and
operation; smaller values use 100. Every round-trip, copy, and corpus-generation
driver invocation has a 300-second wall-clock limit. Override the limit with
`make check RANDOM_TEST_TIMEOUT=<seconds>` when investigating a slow system.
A timeout fails the bundle and prints the command to reproduce it in the log.

Wide-string random filling excludes Unicode surrogate code points and limits
UniversalString samples to U+10FFFF. Values outside that scalar range cannot
be represented as Unicode scalar values in JER JSON strings.
The BMPString and UniversalString bundles exercise this rule through normal
round trips; `check-Unicode-rfill` also covers surrogate-only and boundary
alphabets.

